10483 0 obj
  << /ActualText (In today\031s capital markets\054 the highest\055valued assets are not always the ones generating the most cash\056 Some companies sustain enormous valuation premiums on the back of collective expectations and platform visibility alone \024 with no fundamental change to justify them\056 Digital tokens with no clear revenue model can reach multi\055billion\055dollar valuations within months\056 And even traditional hard assets trade at dramatically different levels of liquidity depending on the story told around them and the category they are placed in\056\n\nThese are no longer edge cases\056 Assets that command prices wildly out of proportion to their revenue models are appearing more frequently and across more sectors\056 The rules by which markets justify price are being rewritten\056\n\nCash flow and intrinsic value \024 the twin pillars of traditional financial economics \024 remain meaningful benchmarks\056 But the era in which balance\055sheet numbers alone could explain market dynamics is fading\056 Prices are now shaped by a more complex mix\072 the narrative an asset carries\054 and the identity it confers on those who hold it\056\n\nThis shift is not confined to speculative corners of the market\056 It now touches corporate cost of capital\054 valuation multiples\054 and whether new businesses gain traction at all\056\n\nTwo forces are driving this transition\056 The first is tokenization)
     /K [ 7 ]
     /P 10490 0 R
     /Pg 1381 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

