10487 0 obj
  << /ActualText (\056 As asset supply \050and information\051 expands without limit\054 the truly scarce resource becomes the finite attention and interpretive capacity of market participants\056\n\nThe result\072 the basis on which markets assign value is moving \024 away from cash\055flow generation and toward the ability to organize an asset into a form the public can understand\054 trust\054 and talk about\056\n\nThis shift rewrites the rules of competitive advantage\056 Companies that can set the interpretive framework first \024 that anchor public trust and enthusiasm inside their own business model \024 earn the right to price at a premium\056\n\nThis report examines that change through the lens of the mediatization of assets\072 why competition is moving from generating cash flows to winning cognitive share\056 It then makes the case for how executives must evolve \024 from traditional asset managers into narrative engineers)
     /K [ 11 ]
     /P 10490 0 R
     /Pg 1381 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

