10502 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Since 1950\054 capital markets have rested on a structural imbalance\072 demand for assets consistently outpaced their supply\056 For 75 years\054 that imbalance was the dominant force shaping markets\056\n\nAccording to a 2025 study by the Federal Reserve Bank of Kansas City\054 \034The Race Between Asset Supply and Asset Demand\054\035 U\056S\056 asset demand rose 415\045 relative to GDP over this period\054 while the supply of assets generated by the real economy grew by only 31\045\056 That gap \024 demand overwhelming supply \024 was the key force that pushed real interest rates down and justified elevated valuations for decades\056\n\nThe environment ahead looks like the mirror image of that world\056\n\nU\056S\056 government spending on healthcare and Social Security currently stands at 11\045 of GDP\056 As the population ages\054 that figure is projected to approach 20\045 by 2100\056 Without major tax increases or structural cuts\054 the resulting deficits will require massive Treasury issuance \024 potentially reaching 500\045 of GDP by century\031s end\056 That dwarfs the roughly 250\045 of GDP in accumulated household savings that might absorb it\056)
     /K [ 2 ]
     /P 10503 0 R
     /Pg 1755 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

