10519 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Once stablecoins and tokenized deposits begin circulating on top of that infrastructure\054 the supply shock is no longer purely a quantity problem \024 it is a velocity problem\056 The 2034 crossover scenario in this report reflects that acceleration\056 Standard Chartered\031s projection of \04430 trillion in tokenized assets by 2034 suggests the scenario is at least plausible\056\n\nThe core question\054 ultimately\054 is not how much more asset supply there will be\056 It is how fast that supply hits the market\056\n\nWhen government bonds and privately issued tokenized assets \024 created at near\055zero marginal cost \024 flood the market simultaneously\054 traditional financial metrics lose their gravitational pull\056 Investors face an endless list of assets with strong free cash flow and clean balance sheets\056 When supply exceeds available capital by orders of magnitude\054 yield and rational revenue models alone cannot differentiate\056\n\nInvestors confronted with millions of tokens\054 all featuring sophisticated structures and seemingly flawless cash flows\054 will hunger for a different dimension of value \024 something that cuts through the noise\056 Owning good assets and building sound financial models will no longer be enough\056 What replaces scarcity of supply is something closer to perfect competition\054 where differentiation must come from somewhere else entirely\056)
     /K [ 0 ]
     /P 10520 0 R
     /Pg 1883 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

