10559 0 obj
  << /ActualText (economic relevance\056\n\nIn a world where attention functions as currency\054 traditional credentials no longer guarantee advantage\056 It is now routine to see Harvard\055trained doctors explaining spinal health in 30\055second YouTube clips\054 or partners at major law firms breaking down divorce law for social media audiences\056 A degree and decades of clinical experience can no longer compete\054 unaided\054 with the reach of an influencer\056\n\nThe same dynamic governs corporate strategy\056 The now\055famous \034Gganbu chicken meeting\035 \024 Jensen Huang sitting down with Jay Y\056 Lee\054 chairman of Samsung\054 and Chung Eui\055sun\054 chairman of Hyundai Motor Group\054 at a neighborhood fried chicken restaurant in Gangnam \024 was\054 by multiple accounts\054 a deliberately staged media performance\056 The event was organized by Madison Huang\054 Jensen\031s daughter and a Senior Director at Nvidia\054 who built the gathering around the concept of an \034AI gganbu\056\035 \050Gganbu is a Korean term for a bond of deep mutual trust \024 the kind of intimate alliance the word implies was the whole point\056 The term gained global recognition through Netflix\031s Squid Game\054 where it appears in one of the series\031 most emotionally charged scenes\056\051 The resonance of that concept\054 combined with the disarming visual of three executives with a combined net worth of \044195 billion casually sharing fried chicken and beer in an ordinary local spot\054 produced a story the internet could not resist\056 Global news outlets and streamers consumed it as content\056 It moved investor sentiment and created measurable economic value\056)
     /K [ 0 ]
     /P 10560 0 R
     /Pg 2749 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

