10653 0 obj
  << /ActualText (quiet reputation\056 But in the attention economy\054 that restraint became a liability\056 Secrecy and caution are invisible\054 and invisible means irrelevant\056\n\nAndreessen Horowitz \050a16z\051 rewrote those norms from the start\056 The firm shaped market discourse through Twitter\054 blogs\054 and media appearances\056 The most celebrated example is Marc Andreessen\031s 2011 declaration that \034software is eating the world\035 \024 a line that broke through the post\055dot\055com skepticism that still gripped the industry and repositioned software companies as the defining institutions of the era\056 a16z also built a dedicated media team\054 hiring editors from the Wall Street Journal and Wired\054 turning itself into what amounted to a \034legitimacy bank\035 \024 an institution whose endorsement reshaped how founders\054 investors\054 and regulators understood entire categories\056\n\nThat narrative power was on display most clearly in crypto\056 When early blockchain companies were mired in associations with money laundering and speculation\054 a16z reframed the technology as Web3)
     /K [ 2 ]
     /P 10656 0 R
     /Pg 4211 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

