  << /ActualText (Even the traditionally secretive world of high\055end real estate has not been immune\056 Location\054 size\054 and condition still anchor pricing\056 But streaming platforms and social media have added a new variable\072 which properties get seen\054 talked about\054 and remembered \024 and which agents become recognizable \024 now materially affects transaction speed\054 negotiating leverage\054 and brokerage profitability\056\n\nThe Netflix reality show Selling Sunset made this explicit\056 The Oppenheim Group\054 a Los Angeles brokerage\054 transformed luxury real estate transactions into ongoing narrative entertainment \024 complete with interpersonal drama\054 competition\054 and character arcs\056 The effect was not trivial\056 Media exposure amplified brand equity\054 focused attention on specific listings\054 and turned high\055end real estate into an object of public desire rather than a purely private transaction\056 The same pattern plays out in Owning Manhattan \050Serhant Group\051\054 Buying London \050DDRE Global\051\054 and The Beverly Hills Estate Agents \050The Agency\051\056 Ryan Serhant has taken this the furthest\054 operating a full in\055house production studio that treats luxury property listings as cinematic content\056 Where secrecy once defined luxury real estate\054 parts of the market are now leveraging visibility to generate liquidity and brand premiums\056)
     /K [ 6 ]
     /P 10660 0 R
     /Pg 4211 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
