10675 0 obj
  << /ActualText (What gets entertainmentized is not the price itself \024 it is the layer of discovery and desire around the asset\056 Properties and agents are now consumed as content and as symbolic goods\056 Competition has expanded from securing better listings to crafting narratives that make the market look\056\n\nTokenization is likely to make this mediatization structural rather than episodic\056 Streaming and social media attached visual desire to real assets\073 tokenization converts that desire into smaller\054 faster\054 more frequently traded financial units\056 Real estate could evolve from a slow\054 high\055friction asset requiring in\055person visits and large capital commitments into a digitally circulated product \024 repeatedly surfaced on timelines\054 shared in communities\054 and accessible in small fractions\056)
