10736 0 obj
  << /ActualText (To make sense of this shift\054 the ideas of media theorist Marshall McLuhan are surprisingly useful\056\n\nMcLuhan argued that the age of print imposed a particular mode of thinking on its users \024 linear\054 visual\054 logical\054 individualist\056 The book isolated readers in quiet rooms\054 trained them to process text sequentially\054 and built the rational\054 individualist foundation of modern society\056 In asset markets\054 the equivalent was value investing\072 the disciplined\054 rational analysis of financial statements\056 One person\054 a spreadsheet\054 a set of assumptions about future cash flows\056\n\nMcLuhan then argued that electronic media reversed all of this\056 Instead of stimulating a single sense in sequence\054 electronic media hit all the senses at once\056 Emotion and intuition gained ground over linear logic\056 Media\054 in his view\054 was not a channel for content \024 it was an environment that restructured perception and social organization\056\n\nFrom that vantage point\054 a stock or token today functions as a media platform\056 The product and service matter\054 but so do the CEO\031s statements\054 the company\031s technological vision\054 and the memes that circulate in its investor communities\056 All of it adds up to a single coherent signal that investors consume\054 share\054 and amplify\056\n\nInvestors are no longer just on the receiving end of that signal\056 They actively spread it\056 The value of a company like Palantir or Tesla is built simultaneously on two levels\072 the traditional layer of fundamentals \024 revenue growth\054 margins\054 technology \024 and a second layer of narrative and identity that the company continuously produces\056 Traditional financial models only price the first layer\056 Actual market prices incorporate both\056\n\nThis is when an asset stops being a financial contract and starts being a medium\056 And the affective premium that medium generates is now among the most significant sources of value in contemporary capital markets\056)
     /K [ 1 ]
     /P 10737 0 R
     /Pg 5467 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

