10755 0 obj
  << /ActualText (When the key information driving prices moves from earnings reports to chat rooms and net\055buy rankings\054 assets stop being purely objects of analysis and become something more like performances\056\n\nIn late October 2025\054 IonQ \024 a U\056S\056 quantum computing company \024 was simultaneously a technology stock and a focal point for Korean retail investor imagination\056 Korean investors held approximately \0444\0564 billion of the company\031s shares\054 roughly 20\045 of its market capitalization\056 The stock had risen about 350\045 from March to its October peak\056 At that peak\054 IonQ\031s market cap was roughly 150 times its annual revenue of \044130 million\056\n\nThe market was not pricing IonQ\031s current income statement\056 It was buying the representative ticker for a future category \024 quantum computing \024 and the story attached to it\056 The asset had become a medium\056\n\nOwen Lamont\054 a Vice President at Acadian Asset Management\054 described this as the \034Koreafication\035 of the U\056S\056 stock market \024 a convergence of market nihilism\054 the pricing of symbolic and political themes\054 and retail investor subculture\056 The operative word is not \034Korean\056\035 It is retail investor subculture\054 which has found its largest and most liquid venue in the U\056S\056 market\056\n\nAs of February 2026\054 data from the Korea Securities Depository showed that Korean retail investors held 94\045 of their overseas equity in U\056S\056 stocks\054 totaling approximately \044166\0566 billion excluding ETFs\056 Research from the Korea Capital Market Institute found that this overseas investment has evolved away from diversification and toward concentration \024 particularly in U\056S\056 tech stocks and high\055risk instruments\056 Rather than dispersing risk\054 it has amplified exposure to specific markets and specific narratives\056\n\nThe Beyond Meat episode illustrates how quickly this concentration can turn into meme\055driven volatility\056 In October 2025\054 Korean investors net\055bought \044180 million worth of Beyond Meat shares in a single week \024 roughly 20\045 of the company\031s market cap at the time\056 Beyond Meat was carrying about \0441\0563 billion in debt and was in the middle of a debt restructuring involving new convertible bonds and share issuance\056 There was no fundamental turnaround in sight\056 Short interest ran from 81\0568\045 to 109\045 as the stock spiked\056\n\nWhat the buyers were purchasing was not long\055term cash flow from the plant\055based protein industry\056 They were buying a compressed\054 high\055intensity narrativeOY)
     /K [ 5 ]
     /P 10756 0 R
     /Pg 5729 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
