10807 0 obj
  << /ActualText (position themselves within it \024 what problems feel urgent\054 what criteria make competitors look weaker\054 what language makes the buyer\031s choice feel justified\056 Strong companies supply the coordinate system of judgment before the judgment happens\056 That is the essence of brand equity\054 and the source of pricing power\054 low customer acquisition costs\054 and high loyalty\056\n\nDoing this well requires quantitative management\054 not just qualitative instinct\056 How fast do messages spread\054 and where\077 How long does attention persist\077 How do organic mentions interact with paid media\077 Are negative reactions structural signals or short\055term noise\077 Narrative must become an operational variable \024 connected to data\054 organizational structure\054 and resource allocation decisions\056\n\nMost existing organizational structures work against this\056 Strategy sits in strategic planning\056 Investor messaging lives in IR\056 External communications are owned by PR\056 Customer messaging belongs to marketing\056 Product messaging is set by business units\056 Each function optimizes for its own metrics\056 But markets don\031t perceive companies by department \024 they perceive a unified entity\056 Telling investors you are a platform company while running discount promotions for customers and delivering a growth story to employees is a contradiction that cannot be sustained\056 Markets eventually price that incoherence as a trust discount\056\n\nWhat is needed is a senior cross\055functional narrative function \024 a team with genuine authority that connects strategy\054 product\054 brand\054 capital markets communications\054 and public positioning\056 This team has three core responsibilities\072 defining and updating the overarching corporate narrative as conditions change\073 ensuring product and business\055unit narratives are coherent with that overarching frame\073 and continuously reading market feedback to recalibrate\056 The goal is not rigid message control \024 it is maintaining a stable central axis while adapting expression and emphasis as needed\056 Narrative is not a static asset decided once and repeated\056 It is a dynamic one\054 shaped by ongoing interaction with the market\056\n\nCompanies are not just producers of goods and services\056 They are designers of how customers decide what matters\054 how investors categorize and benchmark them\054 and how employees connect their daily work to something larger\056 The companies that understand this \024 and organize around it \024 will command higher trust\054 lower cost of capital\054 and greater strategic flexibility than peers with similar assets who don\031t\056\n\nThe competition ahead is not about who can produce more\056 It is about who can design and operate cognitive structures more effectively\056 Narrative architecture is not decoration\056 It is an operating system\056)
     /K [ 0 ]
     /P 10808 0 R
     /Pg 6668 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

