10818 0 obj
  << /ActualText (This report has traced a single\054 fundamental shift\072 the basis on which markets assign value is moving\056\n\nWhen assets were scarce\054 producing and accumulating them was the source of advantage\056 In a world of asset abundance\054 financial soundness and scarcity alone cannot complete a valuation\056 Markets now price assets on how they are categorized\054 who they are compared against\054 and what expectations and trust they project to the people who hold them\056\n\nIn that context\054 tokenization is not simply a new liquidity mechanism\056 It is infrastructure that restructures how assets are surfaced\054 distributed\054 and encountered\056 The attention economy is not merely a media marketing trend\056 It is the structural substrate determining how finite human attention and interpretive capacity get allocated across an ever\055expanding universe of investable assets\056\n\nAs these two forces converge\054 the nature of corporate competition changes\056 Firms must move beyond managing their internal products and capital \024 toward designing the broader context in which they are perceived\054 categorized\054 and valued\056\n\nThat demands a reordering of management priorities\056 Managing a product portfolio and an income statement is necessary but insufficient\056 The firm must also shape \024 consistently and deliberately \024 how investors\054 customers\054 partners\054 regulators\054 and employees read its position\072 what industry it belongs to\054 who it competes with\054 what its results signal about its trajectory\056\n\nThe same technology and the same numbers can read as evidence of structural growth at one company and a temporary trend at another\056 The difference is usually not in the performance itself\056 It is in the interpretive framework surrounding it\056\n\nWhat management must secure is not more noise\056 It is interpretive power \024 the ability to set the terms by which markets categorize\054 compare\054 and evaluate the firm\056\n\nCompanies that achieve this earn higher trust\054 lower capital costs\054 and greater strategic optionality\056 Those that don\031t find themselves evaluated inside frameworks built by others \024 which tends to mean valuation discounts\054 higher cost of capital\054 and shrinking room to maneuver\056\n\nIn the future\054 market leadership will be determined not only by what a firm builds\054 but by whether it can shape how that building is understood\056\240)
     /K [ 1 ]
     /P 10819 0 R
     /Pg 6810 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

